<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tarawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tarawa was fought from 20 to 23 November 1943 on Betio, an islet of Tarawa atoll in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marines stormed a strongly fortified Japanese garrison. Nearly all of the roughly 4,500 Japanese defenders and Korean labourers were killed, and about 1,000 Americans died. The heavy losses shaped later American amphibious tactics in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tarawa.jpg" alt="Battle of Tarawa" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USMC Archives from Quantico, USA · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marines_Advance_on_Japanese_Pill_Boxes,_Tarawa,_November_1943_(10962107133).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
